# Benchmark sources and reference interpreters for the Scheme example.
# fetch.sh clones r7rs-benchmarks into bench/scheme/r7rs-benchmarks/;
# install.sh builds the reference interpreters into bench/scheme/install/
# (sources in bench/scheme/src/). All three are gitignored: nothing from
# these projects is committed, only this manifest, the scripts, and our own
# prelude/postlude/inputs for the harness.
#
# r7rs-benchmarks: Larceny's R7RS benchmarks (W. D. Clinger et al., drawn
# from the Gabriel, Kernighan-Van Wyk and Gambit suites) as maintained by
# ecraven. License: the repository has no LICENSE file (GitHub reports
# none). A few programs carry W. D. Clinger's notice permitting copying
# and redistribution with the notice kept (e.g. equal.scm); most carry no
# license statement at all, so no license is granted for the collection as
# a whole. We therefore only download it at bench time and never commit or
# redistribute any of it.
#
# chibi-scheme: BSD-3-Clause (COPYING in its tree). Release 0.12.
# Gauche: BSD-3-Clause (COPYING). Release 0.9.15, the latest release.
# SLIB: per-file public domain or permissive terms (COPYING). Release 3c3,
# the latest; the suite's Gauche-postlude.scm imports it.
# Guile: LGPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSE). Release 3.0.11, the latest release.
# Guile's dependencies built here too: bdwgc 8.2.12 (MIT-style, LICENSE),
# libunistring 1.4.2 (LGPL-3.0-or-later or GPL-2.0-or-later). GMP and
# libffi come from the system.
#
